earlier in langchain if we wanted to connect a api of ai tool for ex:gemini tool and give it system and user prompt it is the code 

# i wanted to send the input to the gemini api (the packages will changes for the respective api calling ai tool)

------------------------------------------------------
llm=ChatGenerativeAi(model="gemini-flash-3.5-preview") 
#we can choose whatever the model 
-----------------------------------------------------

until above all the code is same but here comes the main thing 

#Earlier they use to write code to send prompt (system and use input)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
prompts=ChatPromptTemplate.from_messages([
{"role":"system","content":"You are a {language} translator , whatever the input user gave you to translate it to the  {language}"},
{"role":"user","content":{userinput}}
])

final_prompts=prompts.format_messages(language="telugu",userinput="i wanted to become a millionaire")
res=llm.invoke(final_prompts)
print(res.content)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

#After that they changed to this code 
previously they used format_messages but now they are using the invoke() 

prompt_value=prompts.invoke({"language"="telugu","userinput"="i wanted to become a millionaire"})
res=llm.invoke(prompt_value)
print(res.content)


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


both the (format_messages) and (invoke) are almost same but the major difference is in "INPUT FORMAT" for i mean for the format_messages it is in "()" where invoke needs in 
dictionary "key":"value" pair format
